For \(1\le H_n\le\lfloor n^{1/8}floor\), there exist constants \(0<c<C<\infty\), depending only on the class radii, such that uniformly over \(\mathbb P\in\mathcal C_n\), \(\kappa_{\mathrm{rec},n}\le C\) and \(c(1+ho_n)\le\kappa_{\mathrm{dir},n}\le C(1+ho_n)\). Moreover, \(c\sqrt{
u_{\min,n}\log(2H_n)}\leho_n\le C\sqrt{
u_{\max,n}\log(2H_n)}\). Hence direct complexity is bounded if and only if \(ho_n=O(1)\). If all shares vanish, direct complexity is bounded; if \(
u_{\min,n}>0\) and \(
u_{\max,n}\le K
u_{\min,n}\) uniformly, then \(\kappa_{\mathrm{dir},n}\asymp1+\sqrt{
u_{\min,n}\log(2H_n)}\).
